# Retired assets. Recordings and drawings that no page asks for any more.
# They stay on disk so nothing is lost and so a rename can be undone, and they
# stay OUT of the repository: 446 clips and 5 drawings are 7.4 MB that nobody
# can reach, and a repository carries its weight for ever.
a1a2/audio/_retired/
a1a2/img/_retired/

# The two frozen variants of the vocabulary bank. The decision they served was
# taken in August. In a published repository they become pages reachable by
# direct URL showing discarded versions of the bank, which is worse than not
# having them. They stay on disk.
a1a2/variant-image-cards.html
a1a2/variant-sentence-audio.html

# The loose drawings under a1a2/img/ belong to those two variant pages and to
# nothing else. No published page references one.
a1a2/img/*.png

# The audio QA report: what a transcriber HEARD back for each clip, against
# what was sent. A build artefact, regenerated by qa_audio.py, useful to
# whoever is cutting audio and to nobody else.
a1a2/audio/qa_report.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- B1/B2 ---
# The same three rules A1/A2 already lives under, applied to book 2.

# Retired clips. One: the u39 dialogue line changed when that slot became the
# full prepositions unit, and the old recording has nowhere to be played.
b1b2/audio/_retired/

# The audio QA report: what a transcriber HEARD back for each clip against what
# was sent. A build artefact, regenerated by qa_audio.py.
b1b2/audio/qa_report.json

# The render signature: model id, voice ids and voice settings. It is what the
# FACTORY needs to know whether a clip is stale, and it is the production recipe
# for this book's sound. It belongs to the kit, not to a public web root.
b1b2/audio/render_signature.json
